      "scope": "Carrier cut, reconstructed cosine/sine amplitudes, density-gradient and advective portions, drive sign, conditions for force identification and finite switch-on. Audit of the two drive locations, three gauges and causal pulse.",
      "verbatim": "The advective/amplitude split follows directly from ψ=A exp(iθ) and the code reconstructs each real quadrature correctly.",
      "disposition": "Reported only actual finite-switch measurements. Added a separate zero-start smooth pulse with reversed half-strength loads; use no steady-phase or travel-time inference.",
      "final_verdict": "Scoped clear on the two-depth displacement and signed phase at s=0.30+0.40i, the canonical +w carrier flux and its two-term split, the conditional one-frequency inverse and cross-mesh auxiliary-force control, and the smooth-pulse displacement, flux and half-endpoint timing."
    },
    {
      "scope": "Archived physical observables, work-conjugate force signs, positive control and conditional ranks of the carrier-only inverse.",
      "verbatim": "Scoped clear for same-model cross-mesh recovery at s=0.30+0.40i",
      "disposition": "Distinguished hidden external calibration forces, inferred material reactions and flux; balanced-drive conditioning uses superposition. The two auxiliary-force errors are example recoveries, not a universal sensitivity."
